    "body": "Echo keeps getting a little better with every update. Not everything here will apply to you, but you'll likely find something you like, whether that's bit-perfect USB-DAC output, a Taste Mix that refreshes itself daily, or Extension Sources for third-party content. Here's what's new.\r\n\r\n## Highlights\r\n\r\n- Play music bit-perfect through an external USB DAC, with automatic sample rate switching.\r\n- Get a Taste Mix playlist that builds from your listening history and refreshes every 24 hours.\r\n- Add third-party content through the new Extension Sources page.\r\n- Get Spotify-based recommendations alongside your YouTube Music home sections.\r\n- Choose your haptic intensity and which interactions vibrate.\r\n\r\n## New Features\r\n\r\n### Audio and Playback\r\n- **Bit-Perfect USB-DAC output:** Send audio directly to an external USB DAC. Supports UAC1 and UAC2 devices, automatic sample rate switching, and hardware or software volume control (#545).\r\n- **Varispeed:** New player setting that links pitch to playback speed for a tape-style speed-up and slow-down effect. When enabled, the separate Tempo and Pitch dialogs are replaced by one Speed dialog.\r\n\r\n### Extension Sources\r\n- **Extension Sources:** Add custom addon server URLs to bring in third-party content. Extension results appear in Search and play through the app's normal player.\r\n- **Settings page:** New Extension Sources screen with site icons and a toggle to enable or disable each addon.\r\n- **Automatic URL handling:** Custom URLs without `https://` are now corrected automatically.\r\n\r\n### Recommendations and AI\r\n- **Local Taste Engine:** Generate playlists on your device from your listening habits. It weighs plays, skips, likes, recency, time of day, and genre (#542).\r\n- **Never recommend again:** New song menu action that excludes a track from future recommendations.\r\n- **Daily Taste Mix:** Create from Taste can now run as a background service in AI Settings. It refreshes your \"My Taste Mix\" playlist every 24 hours instead of creating duplicates.\r\n- **Create from Taste in Library:** Quick-access option in the Library menu, with a short progress dialog.\r\n- **Spotify recommendations:** Sign in under Settings > Account > Integrations and choose your Recommendation Source under Settings > Content > Misc. Spotify carousels appear alongside the standard YouTube Music sections, and fall back to your Spotify top artists if you have no local history.\r\n- **Opper provider:** Opper is now available as an AI provider.\r\n- **API Route provider:** New AI translation provider (#566).\r\n- **Custom AI models:** Enter your own model name when the Custom provider is selected. Completion endpoints are normalised automatically (#562).\r\n- **Test Connection:** Check your endpoint, model, and API keys from AI Settings. Works with OpenRouter and DeepL (#562).\r\n\r\n### Song DNA\r\n- **Wikipedia fallbacks:** Song DNA now falls back to Wikipedia when other sources have no match.\r\n\r\n### Appearance\r\n- **New app icons:** Added the Craft icon by CR3TO_ and the Sadie Sink icon, requested by the community.\r\n- **Circular icon masks:** Custom app icons now support circular masks.\r\n- **Apple Music style player menu:** New menu layout in the player.\r\n\r\n### Haptics\r\n- **Intensity levels:** Choose Light, Medium, or Strong.\r\n- **Individual controls:** Turn Touch, Long-press, Scroll boundary, and Slider haptics on or off separately.\r\n- **Scroll boundary vibration:** Scrolling now vibrates only when you reach the top or bottom edge (#527).\r\n- **Dedicated Haptics menu:** All haptic options moved out of Appearance into their own sub-menu, each with an icon.\r\n\r\n## Improvements\r\n\r\n### Interface\r\n- **Home carousel:** The Quick Picks carousel is taller (360dp), so square album covers are no longer heavily cropped. Titles are larger and bold, and the loading skeleton matches the new size.\r\n- **App icon list:** Icons in settings are now sorted alphabetically.\r\n- **Ambient Mode:** When album art is hidden, lyrics stay centred in a block 60% of the screen width instead of shifting to the edge.\r\n- **Artist screen:** The Subscribe button is now a full pill shape.\r\n- **Extension Sources:** The fallback icon now matches the text colour, and the delete icon is red to mark a destructive action.\r\n- **AI connection test:** A successful test now shows \"Connected successfully!\" as on-screen text instead of a popup. Errors still use a dialog.\r\n\r\n### Home\r\n- **Fresher recommendations:** Quick Picks and Forgotten Favorites now show a different set of tracks on every refresh (#559).\r\n\r\n### Search and Extensions\r\n- **Up Next for addon tracks:** YouTube radio recommendations are now generated for tracks from addons.\r\n- **Better track matching:** Newly searched YouTube tracks are more reliably matched with lossless addon streams.\r\n\r\n### Playback\r\n- **Crossfade:** A new crossfade engine uses an equal-power curve and prepares the next track adaptively for smoother transitions.\r\n- **Metadata cleaning:** Song titles and artist names are cleaned up consistently, which improves lyrics matching. Band names containing ampersands and conjunctions are preserved.\r\n- **Longer AI generation timeout:** Playlist and recommendation generation now waits up to 90 seconds, so complex requests no longer time out.\r\n\r\n## Bug Fixes\r\n\r\n- Fixed playback staying paused after recovering from a network error.\r\n- Fixed a drop in volume after network recovery, caused by the loudness normaliser staying attached to an old audio session.\r\n- Fixed streams cutting off before the end of a track.\r\n- Fixed the play/pause button and progress bar going out of sync during crossfade and background prebuffering.\r\n- Fixed music continuing to play after clearing the app from recents when \"Stop music upon app activity clear\" was enabled. The player now shows the correct button on relaunch (#555).\r\n- Fixed the blur effect not being applied to inactive lyrics lines.\r\n- Fixed generated Create from Taste playlists not appearing in your saved library.\r\n- Fixed Library shortcut cards having uneven heights and unwanted word wrapping on narrow screens (#558).\r\n- Fixed Search needing a double Enter press to dismiss the keyboard.\r\n- Fixed overlapping text in the Extension Sources screen.\r\n- Fixed custom addon URLs without `https://` failing silently.\r\n- Fixed the equaliser processor not being unregistered when the player was released.\r\n\r\n## Internal\r\n\r\n- Version bumped to 1.4.2.\r\n- Reorganised the codebase into separate modules (`:domain`, `:metadata`, `:dsp-core`, `:audio-dsp`) with a deterministic metadata cleaning pipeline (#550).\r\n- Added a Room database migration for play statistics and recommendation exclusions.\r\n- Added a foundational `AiLogger` for tracking AI metrics.\r\n- Indexed more than 40 previously missing settings in settings search, including Discord RPC, Backup and Restore, AI connection tests, Account, Appearance, Player, and Content options.\r\n- Updated ktor from 3.4.0 to 3.6.0 (#512).\r\n\r\n## Contributors\r\n\r\nThank you to everyone who contributed to this release.\r\n\r\n- @iad1tya : Maintainer. Extension Sources, Daily Taste Mix, Spotify recommendations, Song DNA, haptics settings, app icons, Home and Ambient Mode UI, bug fixes, release management.\r\n- @VardhmanSurana : Local Taste Engine (#542), Bit-Perfect USB-DAC output (#545), audiophile pipeline, metadata cleaning and clean architecture (#550), crossfade engine, haptics overhaul (#527).\r\n- @pranav6004 : Custom AI models, Test Connection, and longer generation timeout (#562).\r\n- @DennyHo0917 : API Route AI translation provider (#566).\r\n- @Felixkw12 : Opper AI provider.\r\n- @mrAbhimanyuVishwakarma : Added full suite of Echo home screen widgets",
